- RuleIdentityEl        (191k tested, 0.5k applied)
- RuleAddMultCollapse   (178k tested, 1.4k applied)
- RuleCondNegate        (54k tested,  494 applied)
- RuleConditionalMove   (235k tested,  0 applied — always-fail on top30)
- RuleThreeWayCompare   (51k tested,   0 applied — always-fail on top30)

Each canApply is a faithful pure-read mirror of applyOp's fail path:
- RuleTermOrder: const-vs-non-const input check
- RuleLogic2Bool: isBooleanValue + constant-bounds check
- RuleXorCollapse: opcode-of-input-def + loneDescend + isFree checks
- RuleIdentityEl: input1 constant + opcode-specific identity check
- RuleAddMultCollapse: input1 constant + input0's def opcode == op->code
- RuleCondNegate: just op->isBooleanFlip()
- RuleConditionalMove: inlines checkBoolean logic for each input (avoids const_cast)
- RuleThreeWayCompare: constant slot + bounds check + INT_ADD def check
  (skips expensive detectThreeWay walk; let serial applyOp do it)

Conservative on downstream complex/expensive checks — return 1 (may-apply) so
serial applyOp still runs to do full verification.

