applyParallel: inline phase 1 for small workloads

Add an inline fast-path that skips the thread pool dispatch entirely when
the per-call op count is below INLINE_THRESHOLD (200 ops/worker).  Thread
submit+wait overhead is ~500-1000us for 4-way dispatch; with ~50ns canApply
calls and ~5 rules-with-canApply per op, very small batches don't amortize
the threading cost.

This makes the parallel mode track serial more closely for typical small
functions while still parallelising large ones.

Verified: 664/668 datatests in OFF and DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS=4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Path 2 foundation: MutationScope enum + block conflict graph

Add Rule::mutation_scope enum and virtual getMutationScope() (default
scope_block_global = most conservative).  This will be used by Path 2's
block-level parallel dispatch to decide which basic blocks can be
processed concurrently.

Add block_conflict.{hh,cc} — graph data structure that tracks pairwise
cross-block def-use conflicts plus a greedy coloring algorithm.  Build
algorithm: O(N) over all ops walking output->descend chains.  Coloring:
greedy least-color-first.  Both unused until ActionPool::applyBlockParallel
wires them in.

Verified: 664/668 datatests in OFF and DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS=4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Path 2: add block-conflict graph profiling hook

Add DECOMP_INTRA_GRAPH_STATS=1 env to dump conflict-graph statistics
(blocks, edges, colors, max_group) for each function on first
applyParallel call.  Used to evaluate the parallelism potential of
real-world functions before wiring up block-parallel dispatch.

Top30 libc measurement (33 functions):
  avg_blocks=91  avg_edges=202  avg_colors=4.1  avg_max_group=44
  max_blocks=674  max_group=306
  fns with >=4-way parallel potential: 24 / 33
  100+ block parallel groups: 5 functions

These numbers indicate Path 2 has substantial potential: most non-trivial
functions can be partitioned into 4+ independent block groups, each
suitable for parallel processing within an ActionPool sweep.

Verified: 664/668 datatests in OFF and DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS=4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

