Path 3 step 2: applyBlockParallel skeleton (DECOMP_INTRA_BLOCK_PARALLEL=1)

Adds ActionPool::applyBlockParallel — a new dispatcher that partitions ops
by the block-conflict-graph color of their containing BasicBlock and
dispatches color groups in order.  Still single-threaded in this step;
isolates the contribution of color partitioning so that P3-3 can layer
actual parallelism on a verified base.

Implementation:
- Build + color the BlockConflictGraph once per call.
- Snapshot ops into vector<vector<PcodeOp*>> indexed by color, plus a
  "loose" bucket for ops whose parent block is missing or out of range.
- Walk color groups in order; within each, iterate ops in their natural
  SeqNum order (preserved by beginOpAll() + push_back).
- Each (op, rule) pair dispatches exactly like serial processOp().
- scope-stats counters wired in for symmetry with applyParallel.

BlockConflictGraph gains a colorOf(blockIndex) accessor for inline use
by the dispatcher.

Env gate: DECOMP_INTRA_BLOCK_PARALLEL=1 (additive on top of
DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS>1) routes ActionPool::apply through this path.
When the env is unset, behavior is unchanged.

Op visit order differs from pure SeqNum (color-major instead).  The
ActionPool's iterate-to-quiescence outer loop tolerates this; datatests
remain 664/668 in DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS=0 and =4+BLOCK_PARALLEL=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

Path 3 step 3: color-aware canApply + per-rule stats reporter

Combined two-part step delivering (a) + (d) from the audit plan:

(a) Color-aware canApply in applyBlockParallel
Phase 1 now computes the canApply skip mask in parallel, chunked by
color groups rather than by raw op index.  Each worker takes a
contiguous range of colors; ops within a color group share def-use
locality, so cache misses across worker boundaries are reduced.
Phase 2 stays serial (block-parallel applyOp requires Funcdata thread-
safety not yet in place) but consults the skip mask exactly like
applyParallel.

Inline fast-path when n < 200*numWorkers or totalColors <= 1; otherwise
spawns up to numWorkers tasks over color ranges and waits.

(d) Per-rule stats reporter (DECOMP_INTRA_RULE_STATS=1)
