Path 4 batch 2: Funcdata::poolMutex on allocators + IR mutators (L1)

Adds the lock-hierarchy L1 mutex defined in parallel_safety.hh:
mutable std::recursive_mutex Funcdata::poolMutex.

Wrapped (acquire poolMutex at function entry):
  funcdata_op.cc:
    opSetOpcode, opUnsetOutput, opSetOutput, opSetInput, opUnsetInput,
    opSwapInput, opInsert, opUninsert, opDestroy, opRemoveInput,
    opInsertInput, newOp (both Address and SeqNum overloads).
  funcdata_varnode.cc:
    newConstant, newUnique, newVarnodeOut, newUniqueOut, newVarnode.

Recursive so nested calls (opSetInput → newConstant → bumpIrModCount)
don't self-deadlock.  In serial mode the mutex is uncontended; cost is
one fast-path CAS per entry.

Not wrapped yet (less common, deferred to P4-3+):
