Path 4 batch 3: per-Varnode descendMutex (L2)

Adds mutable std::mutex Varnode::descendMutex.  Acquired by
addDescend/eraseDescend to serialize concurrent mutations to the
descend list (and the setFlags(coverdirty) it triggers).

Cost: ~40 bytes per Varnode on libstdc++/x86_64 — for a function
with 100k Varnodes that's ~4MB extra.  Acceptable for the safety
guarantee on the parallel path; serial-mode behavior unchanged.

Lock order:
  poolMutex (L1, recursive)  is acquired by callers
  descendMutex (L2, plain)   acquired briefly inside addDescend/eraseDescend
  L2 is never held across calls back into Funcdata, and never two
  descendMutex acquisitions are held simultaneously (opSetInput
  releases the old varnode's lock before acquiring the new one's).

beginDescend/endDescend remain unsynchronized (const accessors).
In the planned parallel dispatch, phase-1 canApply is the only
reader and it runs strictly before phase-2 mutators, so there is no
read/write race on the list iterators.

Datatests: 664/668 in DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS=0 (matches baseline).

