Path 4 fixes: ASan-validated race triage + atomic opSetInput

ASan-built decomp_test_dbg under DECOMP_INTRA_TRUE_PARALLEL=1 caught two
classes of unsafe scope_op_only rules and one transient-null race in
Funcdata::opSetInput.

Rule misannotations (scope_op_only -> scope_block_global):
  RuleEarlyRemoval: calls data.opDestroy(op) which delete's the output
    Varnode; another phase-2a worker that picked up the same Varnode as
    input between hasNoDescend check and destroy dereferences a freed
    pointer.  Pinpointed by ASan UAF report.
  RuleTermOrder: inserts new op into a basic block and creates a Varnode
    at a shared (basevn->addr+shift) address; two threads creating
    colliding outputs cause vbank.createDef to xref+delete and return a
    Varnode that the first thread still holds.
  RuleStoreVarnode: creates output Varnode at stack address; also calls
    ScopeLocal::markNotMapped on isStoreUnmapped -- global mutation.
  RuleSegment: inserts new SUBPIECE into the block; Varnode at vn->addr.
  Rule2Comp2Mult, RuleCondNegate, RuleTransformCpool: insert new ops.

Funcdata::opSetInput atomic-pointer-swap fix:
  Old order (opUnsetInput -> addDescend -> setInput) left op->in[slot]
  = nullptr for a brief window.  Phase-2a workers iterating input chains
  observed null and crashed (ASan: Varnode::isHeritageKnown SEGV in
  RulePropagateCopy).  New order writes vn into the slot first
  (pointer-sized atomic), then erases the old descend entry; readers
  always see a valid Varnode pointer.

Stress validation (datatests x 100 iterations, W=4 path4):
  Before fixes:   ~16% iterations SEGV (malloc tcache corruption)
  After fixes:    2% residual (different signature: newVarnodeOut +
                  vbank.xref returning existing Varnode; deeper bug
                  deferred)
  Serial baseline: 0% (clean)

Real-corpus bench (libcrypto 14 heavy funcs, 5 runs avg seconds):
