P4-fix-5: downgrade HumptyDumpty + DumptyHump (non-atomic rewrites)

External consultation bisected the residual libcrypto SEGV under
TRUE_PARALLEL down to a minimal denylist of two rules:
RuleHumptyDumpty and RuleDumptyHump.  Both perform a multi-step IR
rewrite (opRemoveInput + opSetInput + opSetOpcode and the same trio
in reverse) that is not atomic from a lock-free reader's perspective:
phase-2a workers iterating an input's descend list can observe an op
with shrunk input arity but stale slot pointers (or vice versa) and
crash.

Consultation observations on libcrypto:
  Path4 TRUE_PARALLEL, no denylist:      79/80 funcs (death on
                                          EC_GROUP_new_from_params)
  Repeat:                                same death point
  Denylist piece2zext,piece2sext:        not enough — death on
                                          OSSL_HTTP_REQ_CTX_nbio
  Denylist subcancel,shiftsub,
    humptydumpty,dumptyhump,shiftand:    80/80
  Denylist only humptydumpty,dumptyhump: 80/80   <- minimal set
  Denylist only one of the pair:         hang / no progress

Demoting both rules from scope_op_only to scope_block_global so they
run only in phase 2b serial.  scope_op_only is shown by this bisect
to not be a strong enough criterion for true-parallel safety when a
rule performs multi-step mutation; the criterion should be tightened
in a follow-up, or such rules refactored to atomic rewrites.

