P4-fix-6: drop cross-core counter writes from phase 2a hot loop

rl->count_tests and rl->count_apply are uint4 fields on the shared
Rule struct.  Each phase-2a worker incremented them on every rule
iteration, causing cache-line ping-pong across all participating
cores: the same cache line that holds the counter has to be moved
between cores on every increment.  On a 48-core host this dominated
the phase 2a overhead and made path4 net-slower than serial.

Drop both increments in phase 2a.  Stats from phase 2b serial path
remain accurate (still fully counted there); the under-count from
phase 2a is acceptable for profiling counters.  No functional impact.

