P4-d4: Heritage::guardCalls planning/apply split (point-4 hot path)

External profiling (research/point4_profile/POINT4_FINDINGS.md) showed
that Heritage::guardCalls is the dominant hot path in placeMultiequals
on call-heavy functions: 90% of guard, 76% of place, 76% of Heritage,
which is the biggest Action by total wall time.  The cost is the
O(numRanges * numCalls) cross-product loop; on AGXG16X top-5 functions
the sum of call-site scans was 575,763.

Split guardCalls into two phases:

  Phase 1 (parallel, pure-read): for each call-site i, build a
    GuardCallPlan { callIndex, transOffset, isAssignmentSkip,
    tryregister, isOutputActive, outputCharacter, isStackOutputLock,
    stackOutputCharacter, isInputActive, inputCharacter, effecttype }.
    No Funcdata or ParamActive mutation.  Workers fan out across
    call-site indices via the shared ThreadPool.

  Phase 2 (serial, in call-index order): replay each plan via
    applyGuardCallPlan, which does the mutations (tryOutputOverlapGuard,
    tryOutputStackGuard, guardCallOverlappingInput, registerTrial,
    newIndirectOp, newIndirectCreation, etc.).  Iteration order matches
    the original loop, preserving deterministic trial registration and
    op-insertion order — same IR result as the serial path.

Env-gated:
  DECOMP_PARALLEL_GUARDCALLS=1            opt-in
  DECOMP_PARALLEL_GUARDCALLS_MINCALLS=N   threshold (default 64)
  DECOMP_INTRA_WORKERS=N                  reused; phase 1 chunks calls / N

Skips parallel when numCalls < threshold (per-call read cost too small
to amortize thread-pool dispatch).

Validated:
  datatests serial:                       668/668
  datatests + GUARDCALLS=1 (no engage):   668/668
  datatests + W=4 GUARDCALLS=1 MINCALLS=2 (forced engage): 668/668
  datatests + W=4 GUARDCALLS=1 MINCALLS=1 (every func):    668/668

Plan/apply split is provably IR-equivalent to the serial loop: phase 1
captures only read-only decisions, phase 2 replays the same branch tree
in the same call-index order.  The only freedom is that whichTrial()
re-checks happen in phase 2 (using up-to-date state from prior-call
applies) — matches original semantics exactly.

Research artifacts committed under
  Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/research/point4_profile/
including the profile-instrumentation patches, the per-substage timing
summary, the top-functions Java script, and the consultation's
POINT4_FINDINGS.md.

